{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The Stan program has no likelihood sampling statement for any top-level data variable; all top-level data are context inputs used for prior predictive simulation in `generated quantities`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The model block is empty, there are no parameters requiring priors, and there is no protected observation to score.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  real<lower=0> length_scale;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] zeros;
  zeros = rep_vector(0, N);
}
model {}
generated quantities {
  array[N] real x;
  vector[N] y;
  vector[N] f;
  for (n in 1:N)
    x[n] = uniform_rng(-2,2);
  {
    matrix[N, N] cov;
    matrix[N, N] L_cov;
    cov = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, length_scale);
    for (n in 1:N)
      cov[n, n] = cov[n, n] + 1e-12;
    L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);
    f = multi_normal_cholesky_rng(zeros, L_cov);
  }
  for (n in 1:N)
    y[n] = normal_rng(f[n], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 3,
  "alpha": 1.8159007726506036,
  "length_scale": 1.9444981310559026,
  "sigma": 4.922502233805994
}","protected_variables":[]}
